  "method": {
    "app": "benchmarks/twins/composeui_app.py (20 pages, 10 rows per page)",
    "command": "uv run --group browser python benchmarks/idle_sessions.py --output benchmarks/results/idle-sessions-4bbf7d7.json",
    "batches": "Each case opens a first batch of sessions, then a second batch of the same size. 'kept' keeps the first batch in memory; 'hibernated' saves it to disk between the batches. CPython rarely returns freed memory to the system, so RSS doesn't drop after a sweep: the second batch reuses it instead. rss_saved_mib is the kept case's total_mib minus the hibernated case's.",
    "session_idle_s": 3600,
    "hibernation": "After browser requests settle, set idle to 0 for one explicit hibernate_idle sweep, then restore 3600. The natural timer delay is not measured.",
    "memory": "Server process RSS after gc.collect at every snapshot, and Python's allocated blocks (sys.getallocatedblocks); no malloc_trim. Browser memory excluded. Fresh server for each case and repeat, no warm-up.",
    "save": "Wall time of the explicit sweep, excludes the snapshot's gc.collect.",
    "wake": "Sequential browser page.reload until content and persisted input are checked; includes HTTP, restore, rendering and browser work. Not the stale-action HX-Refresh path.",
    "checks": "All sessions/views freed after save; exact LIVE/ON_DISK counts; input value, URL and signed cookie payload preserved for every wake."
  },
